reviewText:
this is a bit of a weird combination. the xbee shield is not usable because it doesn't come with the xbee module itself. i guess i wasn't paying close enough attention when i ordered it. the lcd shield is wired "differently" to the ones expected by the arduino examples. in order to run the examples from arduino, you'd need to change the following line in the examples:
liquidcrystal lcd(12, 11, 5, 4, 3, 2);

to:
liquidcrystal lcd(8,9,4,5,6,7);

i was not planning on writing a review untill i read "travis dockweiler "tdockweiler"" review and a 4 star rating for this totally worthless cans. if possible, just do what he said:- go out and compare the triport to a sennheiser hd580!!! and you will realize that "travis dockweiler" is either a bose employee or is half deff to think the triports are any good!!!

i had these things and my advice is don't waste your money on it. mine got spoilt and i opened it totally up for fun. i actually did not even want it repaired. with the grado in house, there is no way i will ever listen to this superbly inferior product.

if anybody is soo crazy to pay $140 purely for comfort especially considering the pathetic price-performance audio quality, then this can is indeed for you...if everybody were intelligent, this world will not be any fun to live in. you need some folks walking with the triport to poke fun at :-)
